WEBVTT

00:02.419 --> 00:05.422
[♪ epic choral music playing]

00:08.883 --> 00:11.261
[narrator] <i>The True Demon King has died.</i>

00:12.012 --> 00:15.890
<i>The enemy of the world
that filled the horizon with fear,</i>

00:15.890 --> 00:17.809
<i>was defeated by somebody.</i>

00:18.476 --> 00:20.770
<i>To this very day,</i>

00:20.770 --> 00:23.815
<i>that lone Hero remains unknown,
both in name and existence.</i>

00:24.441 --> 00:27.193
<i>Now the age of fear has come to an end,</i>

00:27.569 --> 00:30.780
<i>that person has to be chosen.</i>

00:33.575 --> 00:35.577
[♪ theme music playing]

00:45.503 --> 00:49.007
ISHURA

02:03.039 --> 02:05.917
Mage City

02:05.917 --> 02:10.672
[narrator] <i>Mage City is the satellite city
closest to the New Principality of Lithia,</i>

02:10.672 --> 02:12.924
<i>serving as an outpost</i>

02:12.924 --> 02:16.886
<i>for Aureatia to monitor
Lithia's movements.</i>

02:17.762 --> 02:21.683
Episode 6
Gathering of Factions

02:21.683 --> 02:24.144
[footsteps thudding]

02:35.822 --> 02:37.490
[Hidow] Have our guests arrived?

02:37.490 --> 02:40.160
[guard]
Yes, it seems they arrived this morning.

02:40.743 --> 02:42.412
So I'm the one who's late.

02:42.412 --> 02:46.833
Well, visitors aren't usually the type
to care about good manners.

02:52.630 --> 02:53.923
[door creaking]

02:53.923 --> 02:55.717
- [gasps]
- [door closes]

02:55.717 --> 02:56.843
[breathes sharply]

02:59.721 --> 03:00.847
Sorry about this.

03:00.847 --> 03:03.433
I called you out and yet I was late.

03:03.433 --> 03:05.185
I'm the Twentieth Minister,

03:05.185 --> 03:06.936
Hidow the Clamp.

03:09.022 --> 03:11.774
M-My name is Yuno the Distant Talon.

03:11.774 --> 03:12.901
Back in Nagan,

03:12.901 --> 03:15.445
the Nagan that got destroyed,

03:15.445 --> 03:17.197
I was an apprentice scholar.

03:17.780 --> 03:20.116
I want to thank you for hearing us out--

03:20.116 --> 03:21.784
Let's skip the introductions.

03:22.327 --> 03:24.621
If a new visitor has appeared,

03:24.621 --> 03:27.165
Aureatia must take that into account.

03:27.165 --> 03:29.083
You did well to inform me.

03:29.083 --> 03:30.501
No...

03:30.501 --> 03:32.587
Not at all.

03:32.587 --> 03:34.339
So then,

03:35.173 --> 03:37.550
you must be the Willow-Sword.

03:37.550 --> 03:40.887
[groans]
Do I have to add that to my name?

03:40.887 --> 03:42.430
I'm Soujirou.

03:42.430 --> 03:45.099
Willow-Sword is a pretty good second name.

03:45.642 --> 03:47.685
Anyway, let me get to the point.

03:47.685 --> 03:49.187
[grunts]

03:50.772 --> 03:53.441
The enemy is the former
Twenty-Third General of Aureatia,

03:53.441 --> 03:55.318
Taren the Guarded.

03:55.985 --> 03:57.862
[Hidow] <i>She has a wyvern army,</i>

03:57.862 --> 04:00.573
<i>and is rounding up
magic items and mercenaries.</i>

04:01.157 --> 04:03.701
I want to put a stop to all this
before war breaks out

04:03.701 --> 04:05.787
between Aureatia
and the New Principality of Lithia.

04:05.787 --> 04:08.164
[Hidow] And I want you two to help.

04:08.539 --> 04:11.292
What about the competition
to decide the Hero?

04:11.292 --> 04:12.961
That will come later.

04:12.961 --> 04:16.047
At any rate,
it's the largest event in the world.

04:16.047 --> 04:18.967
[Hidow] Needless to say, only those
of the highest prestige can participate.

04:18.967 --> 04:20.051
[sighs]

04:20.677 --> 04:22.428
[Hidow]
Consider this a test of whether or not

04:22.428 --> 04:24.555
you're cut out to be a Hero candidate.

04:24.555 --> 04:28.101
If you make a significant impact
against the New Principality of Lithia,

04:28.101 --> 04:32.105
then one of the Twenty-Nine Officials
will probably support your candidacy.

04:32.105 --> 04:34.941
Whatever you say.
So long as I get a decent fight.

04:34.941 --> 04:36.109
[worried breath]

04:36.109 --> 04:37.819
[whispers]
S-Soujirou,

04:37.819 --> 04:40.196
Lord Hidow is a very important person.

04:40.196 --> 04:41.739
Try to be more polite.

04:41.739 --> 04:42.824
Uh...

04:42.824 --> 04:44.492
- How do you want me to speak?
- Oh.

04:45.076 --> 04:46.202
How about...

04:46.202 --> 04:50.623
W-We are deeply grateful
for your generous consideration of us,

04:50.623 --> 04:52.542
mere wandering visitors.

04:52.542 --> 04:53.626
How about that?

04:53.626 --> 04:54.711
Sure.

04:54.711 --> 04:58.006
Let's just pretend
that I greeted you like that.

04:58.631 --> 04:59.716
You guys.

04:59.716 --> 05:01.926
You're lucky I'm a tolerant man.

05:02.510 --> 05:05.305
[Hidow] Yuno, this fight against Lithia

05:05.305 --> 05:08.016
holds particular significance
for you, right?

05:08.016 --> 05:09.934
Y-Yes, my lord.

05:10.518 --> 05:11.519
[Yuno] Lord Hidow...

05:12.145 --> 05:14.897
Are you certain that a follower
of the self-proclaimed Demon King Taren

05:14.897 --> 05:19.152
was in the Great Labyrinth of Nagan
on that day?

05:19.152 --> 05:20.653
I'm certain.

05:20.653 --> 05:23.323
His name is Dakai the Magpie.

05:23.323 --> 05:25.408
A swordsman
who carries a blue, enchanted sword.

05:26.993 --> 05:29.662
[♪ uneasy music playing]

05:30.872 --> 05:35.752
Then, did the Dungeon Golem activate
because this man named Dakai the Magpie

05:35.752 --> 05:37.712
entered the depths of the labyrinth?

05:37.712 --> 05:40.840
That is nothing more
than a guess on your part.

05:40.840 --> 05:42.091
[Yuno grunts]

05:43.301 --> 05:47.722
[Yuno] <i>I don't want to simply accept
that tragedy as a mere disaster,</i>

05:47.722 --> 05:49.849
<i>thinking it was all unavoidable,</i>

05:49.849 --> 05:52.727
<i>and blaming my own weakness.</i>

05:53.311 --> 05:54.562
Lord Hidow,

05:54.562 --> 05:56.397
I would like to ask your permission.

05:56.397 --> 05:57.482
[Hidow] My permission?

05:58.066 --> 06:00.151
I'd like to accompany Soujirou.

06:01.152 --> 06:02.278
[Hidow chuckles]

06:02.278 --> 06:03.905
Fine.

06:03.905 --> 06:04.989
Go for it.

06:06.115 --> 06:10.536
New Principality of Lithia

06:14.791 --> 06:16.793
[wind howling]

06:21.547 --> 06:22.924
[wind howling]

06:22.924 --> 06:24.509
If I remember correctly,

06:24.509 --> 06:26.636
she's eating dinner with Taren tonight.

06:38.022 --> 06:39.190
Don't move.

06:39.816 --> 06:41.192
[Regnejee] Move and I'll kill you.

06:42.318 --> 06:43.694
- [Dakai] It's me.
- [gasps]

06:47.031 --> 06:48.074
[soft grunt]

06:48.074 --> 06:50.034
No need to be on guard.

06:50.034 --> 06:51.953
I'm investigating here too.

06:51.953 --> 06:54.038
I have Miss Taren's permission.

06:54.038 --> 06:56.416
I don't remember giving my permission.

06:57.083 --> 07:00.086
And I don't plan to get along
with some daft swordsman.

07:00.086 --> 07:01.712
Swordsman, you say.

07:02.046 --> 07:04.257
[laughs]
Well, you're not alone.

07:04.257 --> 07:07.427
I doubt I could get along
with the likes of some wyvern.

07:07.427 --> 07:08.678
[Regnejee grunts]

07:09.262 --> 07:13.015
[Regnejee] <i>A man like this
can move into attack from any stance,</i>

07:13.015 --> 07:15.059
<i>faster than my Word Arts.</i>

07:15.643 --> 07:16.894
Do you know of diaries?

07:16.894 --> 07:18.646
[Regnejee] Diaries?

07:18.646 --> 07:20.898
[Dakai] Aren't they popular in this world?

07:21.315 --> 07:24.068
You write down daily events in a notebook.

07:24.068 --> 07:27.822
- Did you know Curte keeps a diary too?
- [grunts]

07:29.532 --> 07:31.617
- [♪ tense music playing]
- No, I didn't.

07:31.617 --> 07:34.620
Do you foolish minians
get pleasure out of such a pastime?

07:34.620 --> 07:35.705
I suppose so.

07:35.705 --> 07:39.417
In any case, it seems that Curte does.

07:39.417 --> 07:41.169
[Regnejee] What of it?

07:41.169 --> 07:43.546
[Dakai] There are no letters
written in this thing.

07:43.546 --> 07:46.007
Holes are made at regular intervals.

07:46.007 --> 07:48.342
It's read by touch.

07:48.342 --> 07:50.011
[Dakai blows air]

07:51.762 --> 07:56.058
What would you do if that princess
was recording things like the weather,

07:56.851 --> 08:00.563
or the times she spoke to you?

08:00.563 --> 08:03.316
[♪ tense music continues playing]

08:04.108 --> 08:05.818
Were you deployed today too?

08:05.818 --> 08:08.946
I just got back
from chasing off some rotten outlaws.

08:08.946 --> 08:12.074
I've not got time to mess around
every day like you.

08:12.074 --> 08:15.953
I doubt you're careless enough
to discuss military information,

08:16.579 --> 08:19.332
but it seems
information is leaking to Aureatia.

08:19.332 --> 08:21.167
What of it?

08:21.167 --> 08:23.669
[Regnejee] If you put one finger on Curte,

08:23.669 --> 08:27.173
I'll tear you into nine pieces
and end your life.

08:27.173 --> 08:30.885
Oh, dear,
you think you have a chance of beating me?

08:31.469 --> 08:32.887
[Regnejee] You fool!

08:32.887 --> 08:35.389
[♪ tense music playing]

08:40.436 --> 08:41.687
[♪ music fades]

08:44.273 --> 08:46.484
- [Dakai] Tell me, Regnejee.
- [gasps]

08:47.068 --> 08:48.236
About your swarm.

08:48.236 --> 08:49.737
What's up with that?

08:49.737 --> 08:50.905
My swarm?

08:51.405 --> 08:52.949
What about my swarm?

08:53.324 --> 08:57.787
Wasn't your swarm wiped out
by the True Demon King once before?

08:57.787 --> 08:59.247
[angry grunt]

08:59.247 --> 09:01.457
[tense sting]

09:02.583 --> 09:05.002
[♪ despondent music playing]

09:06.587 --> 09:09.549
[Dakai] Just four years ago,

09:09.549 --> 09:12.009
around the time Curte lost her sight.

09:12.677 --> 09:15.638
How did you build
such a big swarm in just four years?

09:16.222 --> 09:18.516
What would you do if I told you?

09:18.516 --> 09:19.892
Being a minia such as yourself.

09:19.892 --> 09:21.435
Relax.

09:21.811 --> 09:23.980
I still don't plan to do anything yet.

09:27.400 --> 09:29.860
[Dakai] Not to little Curte, or to you.

09:29.860 --> 09:32.863
If you're going to interrogate Curte,
I want to be there.

09:32.863 --> 09:34.407
[Dakai laughs]

09:34.407 --> 09:36.409
[Dakai]
There's no point in interrogating her.

09:36.409 --> 09:38.911
I doubt she'd speak anyway.

09:39.495 --> 09:42.039
Suppose someone had been filling
Curte's head with information,

09:42.039 --> 09:45.376
it's not like she ever saw who they were.

09:45.960 --> 09:48.212
[♪ pensive music playing]

09:50.047 --> 09:52.925
[Regnejee] <i>I must protect my swarm.</i>

09:52.925 --> 09:56.137
<i>Even if Curte turns out to be a traitor.</i>

10:02.435 --> 10:04.854
<i>I will make the right choice,</i>

10:05.605 --> 10:06.689
<i>like always.</i>

10:11.027 --> 10:14.947
Ishura
Commanding Entity

10:15.573 --> 10:17.825
[Curte]
It seems that Regnejee accidentally

10:17.825 --> 10:20.453
snagged my shawl on his way out.

10:20.453 --> 10:23.998
I can't find it anywhere.

10:24.457 --> 10:26.626
I searched my whole room.

10:26.626 --> 10:28.878
That's a terrible misfortune.

10:29.462 --> 10:33.507
[Taren] I'm sure he brazenly denied it,
but you should forgive him.

10:33.507 --> 10:36.427
[Curte] I know.
[giggles softly]

10:44.101 --> 10:45.186
Delicious.

10:45.186 --> 10:46.312
Is that so?

10:46.979 --> 10:48.481
[Curte] Mom.

10:49.440 --> 10:53.110
Don't I keep telling you
not to call me that?

10:53.444 --> 10:55.196
I feel bad for your real mother.

10:56.822 --> 10:57.823
The thing is,

10:57.823 --> 11:02.370
I was hoping you could keep Regnejee
from doing any dangerous work.

11:02.995 --> 11:06.457
Regnejee's duty
constantly puts him in danger.

11:07.041 --> 11:09.669
Will there be a war again?

11:11.295 --> 11:12.421
[Taren] It looks that way.

11:13.005 --> 11:15.174
I'm the self-proclaimed Demon King.

11:15.174 --> 11:18.344
Aureatia don't hold back on anybody
who takes the title of Demon King.

11:18.761 --> 11:20.346
They will send their army.

11:22.306 --> 11:26.227
When that happens, I must protect Lithia.

11:26.894 --> 11:28.854
Yes, I know.

11:31.315 --> 11:33.734
[♪ soft music playing]

11:33.734 --> 11:36.362
[Taren] <i>Ever since I first found her,</i>

11:36.362 --> 11:39.156
<i>she and Regnejee have been together.</i>

11:39.865 --> 11:41.033
<i>Curte wishes to believe</i>

11:41.033 --> 11:44.954
<i>that Regnejee is an angel
who saves people.</i>

11:46.372 --> 11:47.707
<i>That is why</i>

11:47.707 --> 11:51.836
<i>I cannot tell Curte
the truth about Regnejee.</i>

11:54.797 --> 11:57.758
Regnejee doesn't work without me.

11:57.758 --> 12:00.261
Is that why you're sheltering me?

12:00.261 --> 12:01.345
That's right.

12:01.345 --> 12:04.724
You play a crucial role in this war.

12:04.724 --> 12:07.685
Do you think we can ever find happiness?

12:08.811 --> 12:10.604
Are you talking about you and Regnejee?

12:10.604 --> 12:11.689
And you, Mom--

12:12.189 --> 12:13.399
I mean, Master Taren.

12:13.399 --> 12:15.943
If Lithia wins the war and prospers,

12:16.569 --> 12:18.070
and there's no more danger,

12:18.070 --> 12:20.614
then do you think
we can all live in peace?

12:21.866 --> 12:23.033
[Taren] Fear not.

12:23.033 --> 12:25.119
I've never lost a battle.

12:25.119 --> 12:26.829
I am Taren the Guarded.

12:26.829 --> 12:30.416
I'll finish off this little skirmish
with Aureatia in no time.

12:30.416 --> 12:31.542
Mm.

12:33.419 --> 12:35.421
You should go to bed now.

12:35.421 --> 12:36.505
[Curte] Okay.

12:38.507 --> 12:40.801
Goodnight, Mom.

12:42.261 --> 12:44.805
I thought I told you
not to call me that, Curte.

12:46.766 --> 12:49.685
[indistinct chatter]

12:52.271 --> 12:54.940
This place isn't all that great.

12:54.940 --> 12:56.734
You think so?

12:56.734 --> 12:59.653
There were taller trees in Eta.

12:59.653 --> 13:04.533
[Kia] Well, I didn't think there'd be
so many different types of fruit for sale.

13:05.117 --> 13:07.536
The city of Aureatia is even more amazing.

13:07.536 --> 13:09.622
You're lying again.

13:10.122 --> 13:11.373
[soft chuckle]

13:13.626 --> 13:15.711
[Elea] <i>The reason I've come to Lithia,</i>

13:15.711 --> 13:19.048
<i>is not for tourism,
nor is it for Kia's lessons.</i>

13:19.924 --> 13:24.428
<i>The World Word is my exclusive trump card,
unknown to Aureatia.</i>

13:24.428 --> 13:28.182
<i>I must remove anybody who might trace
the link between myself and Kia</i>

13:28.182 --> 13:31.060
<i>before the competition starts.</i>

13:31.644 --> 13:36.065
<i>Even if it requires drastic action,
I must eliminate them at this stage.</i>

13:39.735 --> 13:41.612
[Kia] Who are we supposed to be meeting?

13:41.612 --> 13:43.906
[Elea] An old acquaintance of mine.

13:43.906 --> 13:45.741
We might be talking for a while.

13:45.741 --> 13:49.662
Even so,
it's boring to stay at the inn by myself.

13:50.287 --> 13:52.373
- [Elea] Kia, look at that.
- Hmm?

13:53.249 --> 13:55.000
A ship?

13:55.000 --> 13:58.087
[soft chuckle]
Why don't you go take a look?

13:58.087 --> 13:59.672
B-But...

13:59.672 --> 14:02.800
Play your cards right
and they might let you on.

14:02.800 --> 14:05.177
Really? I'll go see!

14:06.220 --> 14:08.347
I'll be waiting at the park!

14:08.347 --> 14:09.557
Okay!

14:17.147 --> 14:20.150
[footsteps approaching]

14:21.902 --> 14:23.779
[Elea] Sorry for the wait.

14:24.363 --> 14:27.283
[Lana] No, you're right on time, Elea.

14:28.576 --> 14:30.077
[Elea] <i>Lana the Moon Tempest.</i>

14:31.787 --> 14:35.124
<i>Lana is the only one who knows
about the World Word besides me.</i>

14:35.624 --> 14:38.794
<i>She infiltrates Lithia
as a spy for Aureatia,</i>

14:38.794 --> 14:42.006
<i>and she passed on information
about the World Word to me.</i>

14:45.426 --> 14:47.303
It's a shame about the World Word.

14:47.303 --> 14:48.387
[Elea] Yes.

14:48.387 --> 14:51.056
It seems it was just a rumor after all.

14:52.308 --> 14:54.476
I heard a lot has happened
back in Aureatia.

14:56.145 --> 14:57.646
[whispers]
When is Taren's assassination

14:57.646 --> 14:58.731
set to take place?

14:58.731 --> 15:00.024
Hmm?

15:00.024 --> 15:01.650
So you already know about that?

15:01.650 --> 15:03.736
Your ears are as sharp as ever.

15:04.361 --> 15:07.740
I didn't simply wander to Lithia
looking at the clouds.

15:11.660 --> 15:13.954
The target has secured the star already.

15:14.830 --> 15:17.708
I can release
the wyvern deployment records soon too.

15:18.292 --> 15:22.546
[Lana] In my work in Lithia,
I've won over two who are very capable.

15:23.047 --> 15:25.799
Higuare the Pelagic
and Shalk the Sound Slicer.

15:26.133 --> 15:28.510
Competent mercenaries
can spark internal conflict.

15:29.053 --> 15:30.930
[Elea] You truly are formidable.

15:30.930 --> 15:34.558
Of course,
nobody suspects my true identity.

15:35.267 --> 15:37.645
I'm a highly skilled spy, after all.

15:37.645 --> 15:38.812
Yes.

15:38.812 --> 15:41.649
I'm fully aware of your excellence.

15:44.568 --> 15:45.778
- [Kia] Ms.!
- [surprised grunt]

15:47.863 --> 15:50.491
- They didn't let me on the ship!
- [♪ light music playing]

15:50.491 --> 15:52.284
They said
they couldn't let a lone child on.

15:52.284 --> 15:54.078
[Kia] You big liar!

15:54.078 --> 15:56.163
I-Is that right?

15:56.163 --> 15:57.414
"Ms."?

15:57.414 --> 15:58.749
Ah...

15:58.749 --> 16:00.668
So that's the identity you've assumed?

16:01.126 --> 16:03.796
And I suppose she's one of your students.

16:04.421 --> 16:05.506
[pants]

16:06.048 --> 16:07.549
Is this your acquaintance?

16:07.549 --> 16:09.093
Y-Yes.

16:09.718 --> 16:11.637
I'm Lana the Moon Tempest.

16:11.637 --> 16:13.847
A former student of Ms. Elea.

16:13.847 --> 16:15.057
Nice to meet you.

16:18.310 --> 16:20.062
I'm Kia.

16:20.062 --> 16:23.482
Kia, want to come sightseeing with me?

16:24.108 --> 16:26.193
Ms. Elea isn't much fun, right?

16:26.193 --> 16:30.698
Well, there's not much to see here
in this city.

16:31.198 --> 16:32.908
I know a delicious restaurant.

16:33.534 --> 16:35.369
There are dishes you eat with rice.

16:35.995 --> 16:38.664
It's different from bread. You'll like it.

16:39.123 --> 16:40.582
I-Is that right?

16:40.582 --> 16:41.750
In that case...

16:52.761 --> 16:55.055
Kia, are you still awake?

16:55.055 --> 16:57.016
I'm awake.

16:57.016 --> 16:58.100
[chuckles]

16:58.684 --> 17:00.310
[Lana] Just barely.

17:00.310 --> 17:02.021
[patron 1] Come on, you can still drink.

17:02.021 --> 17:05.232
Give me a break, I've got work tomorrow.

17:05.232 --> 17:07.109
[patron 2] Your work's not that important.

17:07.109 --> 17:08.235
[patron 3] Jeez, thanks.

17:08.944 --> 17:11.321
Taren must be a good ruler.

17:11.822 --> 17:12.906
I guess so.

17:13.365 --> 17:14.533
That's exactly why

17:14.533 --> 17:17.703
- she feels she has to do all this.
- [♪ pensive music playing]

17:18.287 --> 17:20.748
If she hadn't been so popular,

17:21.248 --> 17:23.083
things wouldn't have turned out like this.

17:23.876 --> 17:25.711
Lithia's independence...

17:26.670 --> 17:28.756
and Taren calling herself
a monarch happened

17:28.756 --> 17:31.133
because her people wished for it.

17:31.884 --> 17:33.969
[Lana] <i>They felt she was most fit to rule,</i>

17:33.969 --> 17:35.804
<i>and they wanted their own country.</i>

17:36.221 --> 17:38.098
<i>They put that pressure on Taren.</i>

17:38.098 --> 17:40.267
[Elea] <i>Everybody at the tavern</i>

17:40.267 --> 17:44.063
<i>was celebrating like it was a festival,
even with the impending war with Aureatia.</i>

17:44.063 --> 17:45.189
[Lana] Right.

17:45.606 --> 17:48.400
They think they can win so long as
they have the invincible wyvern army

17:48.400 --> 17:49.943
and the undefeated Taren.

17:50.402 --> 17:53.864
The idea that they might be attacked here
hasn't entered their minds.

17:54.364 --> 17:57.326
[Elea] I was taught by Taren
on numerous occasions.

17:57.326 --> 18:00.871
But in the end,
I was never able to thank her.

18:00.871 --> 18:04.291
[Lana laughs]
Don't start feeling sorry for her now.

18:04.875 --> 18:07.795
If we don't kill her,
there'll be full-scale war again.

18:07.795 --> 18:10.422
The True Demon King has died,

18:10.422 --> 18:12.549
yet starting another war
is pointless for everyone.

18:12.549 --> 18:15.052
[♪ pensive music continues playing]

18:15.719 --> 18:18.180
[Elea]
<i>Lana was in a spy guild during the war.</i>

18:18.180 --> 18:20.474
<i>She carried out a lot of dirty work</i>

18:20.474 --> 18:23.060
<i>as a member of Obsidian Eyes.</i>

18:23.727 --> 18:25.437
<i>Even after she came to Aureatia,</i>

18:25.437 --> 18:27.689
<i>she had no choice
but to continue on that path.</i>

18:28.649 --> 18:32.277
Anyway, I'm nearly done
with this awful job.

18:32.277 --> 18:34.863
I'll live in peace in Aureatia.

18:39.034 --> 18:40.410
[soft groan]

18:40.410 --> 18:41.787
Are we back at the inn?

18:41.787 --> 18:43.205
[Elea] Nearly.

18:43.580 --> 18:47.543
I'm a little tired too,
so you keep on sleeping.

18:48.168 --> 18:49.169
[soft groan]

18:50.629 --> 18:51.630
[soft grunt]

18:52.631 --> 18:54.174
You'll be heading to Aureatia soon.

18:54.842 --> 18:57.302
I'll go buy Kia a toy
as a souvenir from Lithia.

19:23.245 --> 19:24.580
[Elea] <i>Now's my chance...</i>

19:24.580 --> 19:25.747
[soft gasp]

19:28.041 --> 19:30.627
[Dakai] According to Miss Taren,

19:30.627 --> 19:32.462
there's an informant in our ranks.

19:32.462 --> 19:33.755
[Lana] An informant?

19:33.755 --> 19:36.300
[Dakai] What if I told you it was Curte?

19:36.300 --> 19:37.843
What if?

19:37.843 --> 19:39.344
It would be a huge incident.

19:40.012 --> 19:42.514
Are you saying
Taren's adopted child leaked information?

19:42.514 --> 19:44.766
That girl was keeping a diary.

19:44.766 --> 19:46.393
Would you believe it?

19:46.393 --> 19:50.105
She used braille.
Even blind people read and write with it.

19:50.480 --> 19:52.399
We have it
in the Distant World I come from.

19:52.399 --> 19:53.775
Is that so?

19:53.775 --> 19:57.863
[Dakai] Normally, one would assume
that Curte is the informant, right?

19:57.863 --> 20:00.282
But that girl believes in Miss Taren.

20:00.282 --> 20:02.743
She would never betray her.

20:02.743 --> 20:03.827
In that case--

20:03.827 --> 20:06.914
[Dakai] It means
there's somebody who enticed Curte.

20:07.831 --> 20:09.791
What a clever idea.

20:09.791 --> 20:13.754
To use a blind girl
by making her record information.

20:15.589 --> 20:18.050
And succeed in making the perfect alibi.

20:18.050 --> 20:20.135
The informant was outside the city
this whole time,

20:20.135 --> 20:23.513
searching for mercenaries
like Shalk and Higuare.

20:23.513 --> 20:25.015
[Lana] What are you trying to say?

20:25.015 --> 20:27.267
You're the one who enticed Curte.

20:27.267 --> 20:30.312
- [♪ dramatic music playing]
- [Dakai] You used to be in a spy guild.

20:30.312 --> 20:33.232
Creating a code using braille
must have been easy for you.

20:33.857 --> 20:34.900
All right.

20:34.900 --> 20:36.401
Where's your evidence?

20:36.401 --> 20:37.819
The transcriptions.

20:39.571 --> 20:41.823
[Dakai] <i>Since you got back to the city,</i>

20:41.823 --> 20:45.285
<i>you've been transcribing the diary
and leaking those transcriptions.</i>

20:45.285 --> 20:49.665
<i>I pinched those transcriptions
before your comrades came for them.</i>

20:49.665 --> 20:51.750
<i>Of course I've already checked</i>

20:51.750 --> 20:55.671
<i>that the same information
had reached the spies of Aureatia.</i>

20:56.255 --> 20:58.674
[Dakai] Well, I'm a bandit after all.

20:58.674 --> 21:02.928
I find every hiding spot,
and there's no lock I can't open.

21:02.928 --> 21:06.056
I'm always telling this to Miss Taren.

21:06.473 --> 21:08.183
Well, what do you think?

21:08.767 --> 21:09.768
Impressed?

21:09.768 --> 21:11.228
[breathes shakily]

21:12.145 --> 21:13.480
[Elea] <i>The situation has changed.</i>

21:13.480 --> 21:15.941
<i>Simply hiding the World Word
won't be enough.</i>

21:19.111 --> 21:21.196
[Dakai] Get in. Miss Taren is waiting.

21:21.613 --> 21:23.115
[breathes shakily]

21:24.825 --> 21:26.827
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

21:29.037 --> 21:32.708
[Elea] <i>If Lana speaks,
I'll be investigated too.</i>

21:33.125 --> 21:35.085
<i>No matter how invincible Kia is,</i>

21:35.085 --> 21:36.378
- <i>I...</i>
- [footsteps approaching]

21:36.378 --> 21:38.547
- [Kia] Ms. Elea?
- [gasps]

21:38.547 --> 21:41.341
What are you doing? I was looking for you.

21:42.467 --> 21:44.261
Lana was taken by a bandit.

21:44.261 --> 21:45.387
[Kia] What?

21:45.387 --> 21:47.806
We have to save her.

21:47.806 --> 21:49.141
- [whip cracks]
- [horse neighs]

21:52.686 --> 21:54.313
W-Wait up, Ms.!

21:54.313 --> 21:55.731
[Elea] <i>Could it be possible?</i>

21:55.731 --> 22:00.569
<i>With Kia's almighty Word Arts,
could one kill Lana</i>

22:01.403 --> 22:03.613
<i>and escape from Lithia</i>

22:03.613 --> 22:04.948
<i>without leaving a trace?</i>

22:06.575 --> 22:08.577
[♪ closing theme music playing]

23:36.540 --> 23:38.625
Translated by Zacarias Hicks

23:39.251 --> 23:40.836
Next: Episode 7
War Commences
